1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,142
A glass of tea at eighty degrees, in a room at twenty.

2
00:00:04,142 --> 00:00:11,077
It cools quickly at first, then more and more slowly, creeping towards room temperature but never quite reaching it.

3
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:17,877
Newton's law says why: the rate of cooling is proportional to how much hotter the tea is than the room.

4
00:00:17,877 --> 00:00:22,513
That is an equation about a rate of change, a differential equation.

5
00:00:22,513 --> 00:00:24,739
Solving it gives the whole curve.

6
00:00:24,739 --> 00:00:26,042
This unit shows you how.

7
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:36,507
Welcome to Class 12 Mathematics, Unit 14: Differential Equations.

8
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:39,995
Six parts.

9
00:00:39,995 --> 00:00:44,019
Order, degree and forming a differential equation.

10
00:00:44,019 --> 00:00:45,646
Separable equations.

11
00:00:45,646 --> 00:00:47,600
Homogeneous equations.

12
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,777
Linear equations with an integrating factor.

13
00:00:50,777 --> 00:00:52,665
Exact equations.

14
00:00:52,665 --> 00:00:56,126
And applications: growth, decay and cooling.

15
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:03,502
A differential equation contains derivatives.

16
00:01:03,502 --> 00:01:08,112
Its order is the highest derivative that appears: here, the third.

17
00:01:08,112 --> 00:01:15,872
Its degree is the power of that highest derivative, once roots and fractions in the derivatives are cleared: here, two.

18
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:17,794
Watch for square roots.

19
00:01:17,794 --> 00:01:26,753
The second derivative equals the root of one plus the first derivative squared: square both sides, and it has order two, degree two.

20
00:01:27,967 --> 00:01:32,903
Going the other way, every family of curves has a differential equation.

21
00:01:32,903 --> 00:01:47,383
The circles x squared plus y squared equals a squared, for every radius a. Differentiate once, because there is one constant, and a disappears: d y by d x equals minus x over y.

22
00:01:47,383 --> 00:01:50,659
One equation describes every circle in the family.

23
00:01:51,867 --> 00:01:53,177
Eliminate the constant.

24
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,481
Lines through the origin: the slope m is y over x.

25
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:02,940
And for A e to the two x, the derivative is twice y itself.

26
00:02:08,533 --> 00:02:10,214
What does a solution look like?

27
00:02:10,214 --> 00:02:13,730
At every point, the equation tells you a slope.

28
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:16,881
Draw a little line there: this is the slope field.

29
00:02:16,881 --> 00:02:21,738
A solution is a curve that follows those little lines everywhere.

30
00:02:21,738 --> 00:02:25,384
Start at the top and follow them: you go round a circle.

31
00:02:25,384 --> 00:02:27,711
Every starting point gives a different circle.

32
00:02:27,933 --> 00:02:34,679
Algebraically: put all the y's with d y on one side and all the x's with d x on the other.

33
00:02:34,679 --> 00:02:36,567
That separates the variables.

34
00:02:36,567 --> 00:02:42,031
Integrate each side, and the circles appear: x squared plus y squared equals C.

35
00:02:43,233 --> 00:02:43,665
Separate.

36
00:02:44,467 --> 00:02:47,636
y with d y on the left, x with d x on the right.

37
00:02:47,867 --> 00:02:53,595
Both are standard forms: inverse tan of y equals inverse tan of x plus C.

38
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:58,131
Divide by tan x tan y to separate.

39
00:02:58,333 --> 00:03:00,899
Each term is a derivative over its function.

40
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,326
So the logs add.

41
00:03:02,326 --> 00:03:08,799
Writing the constant as log c lets the answer collapse to tan x tan y equals c.

42
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,235
One more.

43
00:03:12,033 --> 00:03:17,369
Separate: d y over y equals one minus one over x, d x.

44
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:22,567
Integrate and collect the logs: x y equals C e to the x.

45
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:35,736
When every term on the right has the same total degree, the right side depends only on y over x.

46
00:03:35,736 --> 00:03:37,516
That is a homogeneous equation.

47
00:03:37,733 --> 00:03:40,599
The trick: put y equal to v x.

48
00:03:40,599 --> 00:03:46,430
Then d y by d x is v plus x d v by d x, by the product rule.

49
00:03:46,633 --> 00:03:49,994
Substitute, and every x cancels from the right.

50
00:03:49,994 --> 00:03:50,950
Move v across.

51
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:57,043
Now the variables separate: v with d v, x with d x. Integrate.

52
00:03:57,267 --> 00:04:03,100
Finally put v back as y over x: x squared minus y squared equals C x.

53
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:05,760
Another homogeneous one.

54
00:04:05,967 --> 00:04:13,164
Divide by x; it is a function of y over x. Put y equal to v x: the v's cancel.

55
00:04:13,367 --> 00:04:16,447
Separate, and cot v integrates to log sin v.

56
00:04:16,667 --> 00:04:19,399
So sin of y over x equals C x.

57
00:04:25,967 --> 00:04:30,799
A linear equation has y and its derivative to the first power only.

58
00:04:30,799 --> 00:04:38,114
Write it as d y by d x plus P y equals Q, where P and Q are functions of x.

59
00:04:38,333 --> 00:04:42,981
Multiply through by the integrating factor, e to the integral of P.

60
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:49,991
Then the left side is exactly the derivative of I times y. Integrate both sides, and divide by I.

61
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,204
Why does it work?

62
00:04:51,204 --> 00:04:57,107
The derivative of I is P times I, so the product rule gives back I times the left side.

63
00:04:58,333 --> 00:04:59,398
The three steps.

64
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:01,802
Divide by x to get the standard form.

65
00:05:02,033 --> 00:05:06,651
The integrating factor is e to the two log x: x squared.

66
00:05:06,867 --> 00:05:13,869
Now the left side is the derivative of x squared y. Integrate: x to the fifth over five plus C.

67
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,346
Divide by x squared.

68
00:05:17,367 --> 00:05:18,228
Spot the shortcut.

69
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:23,578
The integrating factor is one plus x squared: the very thing we would divide by.

70
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:30,862
So the left side was already the derivative of one plus x squared, times y. Integrate directly.

71
00:05:32,867 --> 00:05:34,314
Two slips to avoid.

72
00:05:34,314 --> 00:05:39,496
Make the coefficient of d y by d x one before you read off P.

73
00:05:39,496 --> 00:05:43,647
And add the constant before dividing by I, or you lose part of the answer.

74
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:57,416
Some equations are the total differential of a single function u: d u equals M d x plus N d y.

75
00:05:57,416 --> 00:05:59,749
Then the solution is just u equals C.

76
00:05:59,967 --> 00:06:07,403
The test: the partial derivative of M with respect to y must equal the partial of N with respect to x.

77
00:06:07,403 --> 00:06:08,659
Here both are two.

78
00:06:08,867 --> 00:06:16,271
To find u, integrate M with respect to x, holding y fixed, and add an unknown function of y.

79
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:23,659
Differentiate with respect to y and match it to N: g dash is three y squared, so g is y cubed.

80
00:06:23,867 --> 00:06:28,599
The solution: x cubed plus two x y plus y cubed equals C.

81
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,865
Another exact one.

82
00:06:31,067 --> 00:06:34,147
Test: both partials are two x plus two y.

83
00:06:34,367 --> 00:06:38,972
Integrate M in x; matching N leaves nothing for g.

84
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:41,602
So x y times x plus y equals C.

85
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:58,582
A population that grows at a rate proportional to its size obeys d P by d t equals k P. Separate and integrate: P equals P nought e to the k t.

86
00:06:58,582 --> 00:07:04,940
A municipality had forty thousand people in twenty sixty eight and fifty thousand ten years later.

87
00:07:05,167 --> 00:07:09,999
So ten years multiplies the population by five quarters.

88
00:07:09,999 --> 00:07:16,549
Another ten years multiplies by five quarters again: sixty two thousand five hundred.

89
00:07:16,549 --> 00:07:17,763
No need to work out k at all.

90
00:07:18,967 --> 00:07:19,648
Doubling time.

91
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:24,505
Doubling in three hours means e to the three k is two.

92
00:07:24,733 --> 00:07:27,971
Twelve hours is four doublings: sixteen times.

93
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:30,715
Back to the tea.

94
00:07:31,233 --> 00:07:36,104
Newton's law: the excess over the room decays exponentially.

95
00:07:36,104 --> 00:07:37,462
It halves in ten minutes.

96
00:07:37,667 --> 00:07:43,718
After twenty minutes, it has halved twice: fifteen degrees above the room, thirty five.

97
00:07:43,933 --> 00:07:49,777
For thirty degrees, the excess must fall to ten: about twenty five point eight minutes.

98
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:53,770
Pause and think.

99
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:05,912
Order two, the second derivative; degree three, its power.

100
00:08:05,912 --> 00:08:08,555
The fourth power belongs to a lower derivative.

101
00:08:10,533 --> 00:08:10,968
One more.

102
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:24,789
x: e to the integral of one over x is e to the log x, which is x.

103
00:08:26,967 --> 00:08:28,023
Quick recap.

104
00:08:28,023 --> 00:08:32,893
Order and degree, and forming an equation by eliminating constants.

105
00:08:32,893 --> 00:08:35,380
Separate the variables when you can.

106
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:43,700
Homogeneous equations: put y equal to v x. Linear equations: multiply by the integrating factor.

107
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:46,331
Exact equations: find u.

108
00:08:46,331 --> 00:08:50,284
And the exponential laws of growth, decay and cooling.

109
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:56,604
That was differential equations.

110
00:08:56,604 --> 00:09:01,239
Next, computational methods: solving equations numerically.

111
00:09:01,239 --> 00:09:01,788
See you there.

